// A DS18B20 whose ROM id is a string #param -- set per node, kept by /save --
// lists back by the param's name, and its temperature reads through a #field:
// signed, 1/16 degree, little-endian, as the device sends it. The host has no
// bus, so tests/unit/onewire.dat writes the raw value where a reading lands.
#param  UteRom string = "28-ff-64-1f-07-16-a3-c2"
#buffer Ute:2 in onewire 0:5 UteRom
#field  UteRaw:16 Ute[0..15]
#variable UteC = 0
UteC = UteRaw * 5 / 8
